<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  updatePeriodMillis is the floor Android enforces anyway (30 minutes) and is
  the fallback, not the mechanism: the app calls updateAll when the diary
  changes, so logging a watering refreshes the widget immediately.

  Both previewLayout and previewImage, because one is not enough. With neither,
  the launcher's picker falls back to the app icon, so ThirstTrap showed a green
  square with a droplet in it while every other app in the list showed what its
  widget actually looks like. previewLayout is the modern one and is API 31 and
  up; previewImage is the old drawable, and it is what a launcher uses when it
  either predates 31 or ignores previewLayout, which HyperOS appears to.

  The image is dark-scheme only. A single drawable cannot follow the system
  theme, where the layout can, which is the reason to keep both rather than drop
  one.

  Four cells wide, two tall, and the minimums match: 250dp and 110dp, which are
  the 70n-30 values for 4 and 2. minHeight used to be 58dp, the one-cell value,
  while targetCellHeight said 2, so the widget called itself 2x2 and declared a
  2x1 minimum, which let it be dragged shorter than its content fits in.

  It was 2x2 and is now 4x2 because the content is a list: up to three plants,
  each a name over a line saying why it is asking. Two cells of width is not
  enough for "drier than you water it" at 11sp, and HyperOS also scales the
  picker's preview in proportion to the cell span, so a 2-wide widget gets about
  half the tile and looked tiny next to the 4-wide ones. Wider is both truer to
  the content and better in the picker.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:description="@string/widget_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_watering_preview"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/widget_watering_preview_image" />
